of ice at the soldier and  threatening him with derogatory names  white fled to the local custom house  loaded his gun and pleaded for the  soldiers inside to come to fend him not  far from the scene a second mob had  assembled and began pelting a group of  soldiers with ice and snowballs forcing  them to retreat into their barracks  meanwhile a third more dangerous mob  nearly 200 strong and carrying clubs had  formed in doc square they rang the fire  bells to draw more civilians into the  streets and began to march towards the  Custom House the officer of the day  Captain Thomas Preston was in a  difficult spot if he didn't organize his  troops  the mob might kill Hugh white but  sending out more men would put them all  in trouble and potentially escalate the  situation even further after almost half  an hour of thinking Preston decided the  only thing to do was rescue white the  captain and seven other men marched out  forced their way through the crowd and  stood by the terrified soldier now they  were stuck the mob which had grown to  over 300 was pressing in and throwing  ice chunks of coal  hoist er shells anything they could get  their hands on one man named Crispus  Attucks grabbed a soldier's bayonet and  knocked him to the ground as the man got  back to his feet he yelled at the other  soldiers to fire even though he had no  authority and thus began what became  known as the Boston Massacre Crispus  Attucks was shot twice in the chest  another man was quoted to have been shot  in the head as he stood with his hands  in his pockets leaving a hole the size  of a man's hand all told five civilians  were killed and another half dozen  injured before captain Preston by his  own account was able to get his men  under control to make a long story short  Preston and his men were arrested and  held for trial  over the next seven months various  accounts of the event began to pop up in  newspapers across the colonies and  especially in London each one skewing  the facts to present an argument against  the other side the Bostonians wanted the  British soldiers out and somewhat  surprisingly though after considerable  public pressure the British agreed the  morning after the soldiers were arrested  a local visited future President John  Adams then a Boston Attorney and begged  him to represent the soldiers at their  trials despite the considerable risks to  his reputation and his career Adams  agreed as he felt that every person  deserved a defense the trial would be  interesting for a number of reasons  first it was an intensely politically  charged event notable figures such as  Samuel Adams and John Hancock were  thoroughly opposed to British occupation  and the incident undoubtedly led to more  extreme ideas second it was the first  recorded use of the dying declaration  exception to the rule that excludes  hearsay evidence one of the victims of  the shooting  Patrick Carr lived for a short time  after the incident and told his surgeon  that he forgave whoever it was that shot  him and that the British had acted in  self-defense  in the end despite much anger and heated  debate outside the courthouse the  soldiers were all acquitted of murder  and only two of them were punished by  branding Adams his closing statement was  brief and poignant and it's worth  repeating here he said facts are  stubborn things and whatever may be our  wishes our inclinations or the dictates  of our passions they cannot alter the  state of facts and evidence  nor is the law less stable than the fact  if an assault was made to endanger their  lives the law is clear they had a right  to kill in their own defense if it was  not so severe as to endanger their lives  yet if they were assaulted at all struck  and abused by blows of any sort by  snowball's oyster shells cinders clubs  or sticks of any kind this was a  provocation for which the law reduces  the offense of killing down to  manslaughter in consideration of those  passions in our nature which cannot be  eradicated to your candor and justice I  submit the prisoners and their cause  despite the tragedy and despite the  nearly universal hatred of British  occupation in Boston John Adams stuck to  the principles that all of us should  strive to hold a respect for objective  evidence the law and rational thought  the legacy of the Boston Massacre has  been controversial even down to the name  was it really a massacre if the mob  incited the violence then again was  shooting into the crowd really the only  option the incident raises important  questions even today nearly two and a  half centuries later America was founded  on the right to peaceful assembly and  while the crowd in Boston was certainly  not peaceful at what point does it  become acceptable to shoot civilians  self-defence is a valid argument and  will generally hold up in most modern  court cases but should there be more  repercussions for the use of deadly  force especially by those who have  access to more lethal weapons like the  police and the military from the  civilian standpoint it would appear that  the only way to affect change is to  resort to violence and the civil unrest  that sparked the American Revolution  would seem to support that idea what  does that say about modern protests our  peaceful assembly is still effective  order those calling for more drastic  actions have the right idea what would  happen if police killed a handful of  protesters in 2018 would the legal  outcome be the same even with the  drastically lopsided difference in  firepower we can often gain key insights  into how society will respond to certain  events by looking to the Past and seeing  how our forefathers reacted in today's  polarized and volatile social landscape  a bit of historical perspective might be  a good thing what do you think is  violence against protesters ever  justified or on the other side is  violence against law enforcement ever  justified was John Adams right in  defending the soldiers who killed those  five people what do you think would  happen if there were a second Boston  Massacre today let us know your thoughts  in the comments below and if you really  have a lot to say about the issue why  not compile all your thoughts on a  beautiful new website from Wix with Wix  you can build amazing  professional websites for just about any  application Wix can handle any project  you throw at it whether you want to host  videos share your photo gallery book  clients sell products or just about  anything else you could ever want  whether you need a professional website  for your own personal use or for  e-commerce music hotels or restaurants  Wix does all the heavy lifting like  hosting custom domains email marketing  and more allowing you to focus on the  creative side of things you have total  creative freedom over your websites  allowing for limitless possibilities and  you don't even have to be a web designer  Wix caters to everyone regardless of  skill level so whether you're a novice  business owner or seasoned website  builder if you want to build your very  own professional website visit Wix by  following the link below
 

